editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:69:  **Win sentence, verbatim.** Oryn sets and knits the leg and is grey for a quarter-hour. The healers nod. Teague's arm: "That's a fact about a line." / "Noted" / "Everybody says that now." Brom's week of colours.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:70:- **The Span itself (noon).** An arch on two piers over the sink. Carvings on the piers' inner faces, copied. No steps: the arch is walked as a road rises. The bearing runs "Through". **Nothing happens on the crown.** The thirteenth listens and the ribs know the cost. **The log, verbatim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:72:  - **The lamps finding, verbatim.** Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" / the ruler rule. Two pages. Vastin's third "Noted." **Cael does not add his own third page.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:73:  - **The directive and the objection, verbatim.** "That's a crack." The seals are unnamed. "The Compact … Yes. Part of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:76:  - Seln on the pass: "I looked at it." **The close, verbatim.**
     1	# Movement brief 008 — The Sunken Span
     2	
     3	- PWA book id: fractured-path/book-08-before-the-paths (Monroe 1.3 edition)
     4	- Series id: fractured-path
     5	- Author: Opus (Claude Opus 5.5)
     6	- Chapters: 47–53 (7 chapters) → `manuscript/chapter-47.md` … `chapter-53.md`
     7	- Word budget: ~35,000
     8	- Owner names: no new names. The watch is faceless. Teague's crew stays unnamed.
     9	
    10	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 1 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Teague's spear is a tall MAN** (he / him): the locked Book 7 wrote him so (ch25, ch51, ch52), and Book 8 follows its own edition (OWNER-pending #59). Where the plan says "the tall woman", read "the tall man"; his silence toward the six until his question at the pass stands. (2) **Teague can read** (locked Book 7 ch25: he read a slip twice). Never write that he cannot; if he does not read a sheet it is because it is not in front of him or he has no need. (3) **Lira's asking:** she asked Oryn once about the ankle on the mountain in Book 7 and asked nobody for anything from then until Thornwater; do not call Thornwater her first ask since Norhold. (4) **The stroke and bar** is on stake thirty-two (the Stair's newer stake and the kit's unused one) and on the fourth site's thirty-four ONLY; stakes thirty-one and thirty-three do not carry it. Later records may show the grade on survey SHEETS; the field stakes do not all carry it. (5) **The cord:** the kit's cord is twenty strides, knotted at the fives (four knots to a length); Book 7's Ring was sixty-two cords and twenty strides round. The court is about 1,107 yards across, which is about FIFTY cords, not 159. Give no yardage for a cord. (6) **"West"** was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th (Karis's protected "It's west… Treswick…" speech, printed once in ch6). (7) **Deployment since the Line is twenty-nine** at the end of Movement 1 (two uses of the Iron read in earnest); trials are not counted.
    11	
    12	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
    13	
    14	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 3 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Deployment since the Line is thirty-two** at the end of Movement 3 (one Ember grain and one Wind burst away, both at the cut on the 279th). Ten fragments; the eleventh has not come; nothing came of standing two feet from Vastin's wall. Purse 138 marks. (2) **Iron Wall has been shown once** (the cut): a plane from a line struck with the stick, wall to wall, rooted — he may not lift a foot — loud to anything that hunts a Path, and it spent him to the floor. **Vastin's RIGHT knee** was bitten there; Oryn shut the holes and bound the joint with laths for a month from the 279th (stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall); he said "I cannot undertake" and has kept it to the letter. Brom's right foot, two toes, ten days from the 279th. (3) **The date:** Cael and Seln each know that the technician's sheet carries the day of Cael's Kindling. Neither has said or written it; neither knows what the other made of it; nobody has interpreted the sequence. No figures are ever printed, no span of years is computed, and there is **no second calendar or offset** (one registry reckoning only). Vastin does no date arithmetic and knows nothing of it. (4) **The records at the spring:** Karis has matched FOUR sign-groups to the hide and has given NO number of places; no fifth place has been described. The same stroke and bar stands in a ruled square on all four matched places' sheets (in the field: stake thirty-two and the fourth site's thirty-fours only). The remark "Behaves as device. Cannot be." is on the Stair's sheet in the fourth row; its hand is NOT identified. The instruments column reads true on every line. (5) **Seln has taught one thing, to Vastin** ("Draft nothing. Just look."). Cleon has been named (by Karis) and nothing more is known of him than her protected lines give. (6) **Oryn** went north from the fork on the 281st with the brown mule, her linen and her crossbow with one bolt; Millrace in three weeks; she owes Cael the reading ("the one thing I'm walking up that road owing"); the station term is written in the log. Her past as told at the fork: a house for the sick in a city inside the Line, the column for the patient's tier, a woman from the river sheds mended off the sheet; she has not been through a gate since. (7) **Loads:** boxes on Brom (good shoulder), Lira (both arms) and Cael; the tarred kit case on Vastin, taken up unasked at the fork-stone; Karis the flat and the hide, with the copied page in oilcloth in her coat. **Cael laid his hand on that page once, on the rise.** Vastin has walked beside Cael since the rise. (8) **Stillhounds:** a den that has learned a road runs to where a declaration ends (Karis's sixth line). The sixty yards of four-strand rope are still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman.
    15	
    16	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 4 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Who is where on the 284th:** inside the iron door are Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Karis, with three boxes, the tarred kit case, the flat and the hide; Cleon let them in, counted loads and not people, and shut the door. The unnamed yard clerk is outside; **Seln is above ground, NOT on the card or the count**, watching who comes to the door. Oryn is two gates north with the brown mule. (2) **The count:** Karis is the card's unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands, entered by count; the clerk asked nothing and wrote *four*. None of the four restricted names has been written anywhere; the asset-restriction is still pending. Cards are good only for the day written on them and are torn at each gate; Iron passes the second wall and Bronze the third by right, on a certificate that is read out and written. The way to the registry's yard is the load lane under the third wall and a cut of **twenty-two steps in five flights, a stride and a half wide, walled three men high with no door or window**; it never crosses the square. Cael has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; Lira keeps the same discipline unasked. (3) **Cleon's terms** (given at the cook-house on the 283rd): all the sheets, in their places; they come down to him; no names (his is on the card and is never said aloud by him); **nobody tells him what the sheets are or how old until he has looked**; one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says; no other carried light and no fire of anybody's. He has seen one drawn sheet and knows there are three places and fifty-two sheets, older than what the Compact found; he has not noticed Cael. **His Path has not been shown.** "Rune Path. Bronze." is all that is known of it, from Seln. (4) **Cael:** ten fragments; deployment thirty-two; the fourth and fifth self-readings were made on the 281st, round the still place and not in, uncounted; Tide feels only what flows and returned nothing ("a cord on a stone… *no length*"); he needs an instrument for what does not move, and owes Oryn the telling at the mill. Lira has read the log. (5) **Vastin and Cael:** Vastin has told him why he declined the second reading (the Ostrand case, causal; and a private relief at never learning what a plate would say); Cael has told him that the place was read twice and returned nothing, and nothing of what reads. Ground, not friendship. Vastin carries three sheets under one seal that he will not show; he has sat three times; his right knee is day five of thirty on the 284th (stick; no kneeling, running or wall) and he caught a slip on the steps with his left hand. Brom's two toes: five days left on the 284th. Lira's arm: day nineteen out of wool; her registry paper unshown; the ladder did not pull. (6) **The inn:** the long loft over the stable, by the yard half-door (the painted door has a book), for a week from the 282nd, pot at dusk, seven bowls; **purse 136 marks**. The outer gate counts feet on a bead-frame and writes no name. (7) **Stone:** the grey bridge, the registry's three lowest courses, the undercroft's end and the iron door's frame are one dark dry-laid stone older than the walls; Karis has seen it and stated no conclusion beyond "the bridge was first". The iron door has no lock or handle outside; the clerk knocks. (8) The sixty yards of four-strand were priced at the rope-walk and are to be bought going out.
    17	
    18	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 5 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Eleven fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two; purse 134 marks** at the end of Movement 5 (the night of the 290th). The eleventh, Iron-Wall-adjacent, came from Vastin in the alley's quiet minute; it did not fill, it *set*; its prompt is *This far?*; it has not been deployed and **Vastin has not been told** (Cael holds that as a debt he cannot yet pay; Lira has read the log). (2) **How acquisition lines are printed in this book:** the protected "Fragment eleven" and "Fragment twelve" units are CAEL'S OWN cataloguing of what he reads — set once, in italics, framed as his plain words; they are NOT printed as a system block and take no FRAGMENT ACQUIRED heading or code fence. (3) **The Deepstacks:** an iron door with a sliding bar inside; twenty-seven steps in three flights of nine; three galleries. Middle gallery about 110 strides, Cleon's sloped desk and fixed lamp at its end, a shelf above it with a jar, a tied bundle ("Paper. Not stone.") and the black oak plank's sacking; the fifty-two sheets on three tables, 11/29/12; the plank stands against the third table. Eastern gallery: the old town's tall tally-books. One CARRIED lamp, Cleon's, held "a hand to the left" (Cael holds it and has begun to put it where the eyes are about to go). The boxes go up at the clerk's bell and come down each morning on a fresh card; the clerk writes *The same* and *four*. (4) **Cleon** knows Karis's name (he heard Brom say it and has used it once); his own is on the card and has never been said aloud. He has shown his Path from OUTSIDE only (bear / carried / nothing; "They're orders."; "Same make."; the limit: it does not work on a river, a man or a tree, and costs his eyes for an hour). **His week runs from the 287th to the 293rd.** He has not noticed Cael and knows nothing of the alley or the mechanism. (5) **Karis** has fourteen of twenty-three letters and reads numbers and number-words only; seven kinds bear, twenty-three are carried, eleven are nothing; the bundle is tied and unread; Vastin's copied page is in her coat, unshown to Cleon. Her LEFT palm has seven stitches of Brom's under a strip of his shirt; she writes with the right. (6) **Vastin:** his right knee went again in the alley on the eleventh day of Oryn's thirty (a wall on it against her order, which he heard and asks that she be told); re-splinted with a slat from Brom's box, twice its size; on the night of the 290th he cannot stand or hold a bowl. He gave his name, rank and office aloud at the yard hatch on the 285th; nothing of it was written. He still knows nothing of what Cael carries. (7) **Brom:** the left (good) shoulder wrenched under a dray on the 286th and worse after the alley; he carries his box on the bound right shoulder, a debt entered for the mill's healers; the broker's offer (a guard's post inside the second wall) was answered "I'll think on it." and declined in fact. Lira: day twenty-five out of wool on the 290th; a bruised right shoulder; she drops from heights without the arm. (8) **Seln:** a registry clerk knows his face and voice (the price of a truthful answer at the hatch); he watches from the roof above the cut. His case is **SHUT** — never "unopened" (this edition's Book 6 opened it for the five) — and its contents are named nowhere in this book. He has seen one watcher three times (horseman's boots with the spur-rests cut away). (9) **The faction** (six, hooded, no faces, no Path opened) knows the loft and has shown that it knows; it saw Vastin's wall, a rock, a knife and a boy who stood still, and nothing of quiet ground or the fragments. Cael has ruled that the cut is not climbed at dusk again. The loft is paid to the 295th.
    19	
    20	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 6 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two.** The twelfth is **Rune-adjacent, from Cleon** ("given, not taken"), acquired at his "There," on the 291st; it gives single words (*goes*, *sits*, *bears*, *nothing*), reads made things only, and costs the eyes afterward. Its lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics in Movement 6 and never reprinted. (2) **How it behaves:** it leans at every made thing, unbidden and OUTWARD, and Cael is learning not to look; it has never been used on a person, the crown or the leaf, and **never turned inward**. He refused the inward turn once, deliberately, until Oryn has been asked. **The first inward turn is unbidden, at Millrace, under Oryn's deep reading** (*still*, then *set*); the deliberate inward turn belongs to the plain's edge in Movement 9. (3) **Who knows the twelfth:** Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon. **Not Oryn (owed at the mill, with the readings round the place); not Vastin** (who also still does not know the eleventh or the mechanism). **Cleon's warning** ("If that fragment ever reads something for you that shouldn't be *made* and reads it anyway — …") is known to Cael and Cleon only and is in no book; Cael tells nobody. (4) **The leaf** was read aloud once by Karis and heard by Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin; Lira, Brom and Seln read her copy; Oryn has not heard it. **Nobody quotes the leaf's wording again.** The reductions that may be said: *made*; *for a kind*; "the Architect" as a **title** (historical comparison only — "as old as the Architect" — never a present agent); "four hundred years" only where this packet's plan fixes it. (5) **The chronicle's line is marked and nobody speaks of it again**; the hole is never glossed. **Nobody joins the leaf to the lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; no *terminal*, *circuit*, *infrastructure*; no light, plate or instrument is said to attend, notice or want. (6) **Pole two was said aloud at the yard fire and is not in the log.** The line of march from it: "a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine" — "I want to stand in the middle of it." (7) **Seln's case is on his chest, shut, contents unnamed; he keeps it "a while longer".** Closed chapter 18 says he has carried it twelve years; print no other count. He will not follow the cut boots again and expects them on the road east. (8) **State at the night of the 293rd:** purse **130**; the reserve sealed in the third box; loft and handcart to the 295th; sixty yards of four-strand still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman; Hesk's dividers and note shut in Hesk's book (never opened on a distance); Karis's fair copy in Cael's coat, the other in her notebook; the skin leaf under Cleon's jar and going to no counter; its back (a list of parts) unread — Cleon's work for the 294th. **Vastin: right knee day fourteen of thirty on the 293rd**, slat-bound, stick, no kneeling, running or Wall; he sleeps in the stable's end stall and rides the handcart. Karis's left palm stitched (Brom's seven); Brom neither arm above the elbow; Lira day twenty-eight out of wool on the 293rd. (9) **Oryn** watched a Kindling at her fourth gate, is two days behind, will not come late to the mill, and means to read Cael "as deep as she went", asked first.
    21	
    22	> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 7 audit, 2026-10-12 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two; purse 127 marks** at dawn on the 299th (130 less two for the rope, less one for meal at the mill; the rope debt to the Lowmarch ferryman is paid). Force was SEEN on the 298th (Teague, at a sunk salt cart: heel to palm in one line, a body's length, the recoil down the same line to the wrist) and **not acquired**; "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice." is Teague's. (2) **The contract** (all Teague's words: "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall."): the ten are Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man with the spear, the bow (a broad man with a bad hip), the young one. **Neither healer is on it.** Shares and costs by the count; **the field is Teague's**; the reading is Karis's ("You'll be asked."). The wall is under a healer's month and is not stood before the month is out. **Teague's four know:** a survey was read at Treswick and gave a bearing; the four ages and "three days past the iron"; that an old man's wall stood in a cut. **They do NOT know** the mechanism, any fragment, the leaf or the list, the date, or who Vastin was. The tall man, the bow and the older healer (a lean old woman with a staff and a board) have not yet spoken to the six. Teague has not yet said "Noted". (3) **March order (Teague's):** Seln ahead; the tall man; Teague, with **Cael at his left shoulder a stride back**; Lira; the young one, watching her feet; Karis, the two healers and the mule in the middle; Brom; Vastin a stride behind him; the bow last. Four hand-signs, Lira's: flat hand *stand*; fist *seen*; two fingers *come on*; hand turned over empty *nothing*. (4) **Vastin: day twenty of thirty on the 299th**; Oryn's linen and two laths; stick; **he walks in the file from the ford** (he rode a tail-board on the level from the 295th to the 298th and walked the hills and the cut). He has said "Noted" twice (the grade; the knee) — it is Cael's word and he says so. He is on the contract's count as one of "your six"; he has not asked to join the six and nobody has spoken of it. He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh (his own), the twelfth, the two words or the date; he knows that he is not told and that it is "six people's". (5) **The grade:** three marks — a stroke alone (a box ruled and EMPTY; no first-tier site exists on any sheet); a stroke with one bar (the four places; stake thirty-two; the dead surveyor's book); a stroke with two bars (six sheets of a fifth place). "A mark is a grade … what he's *for* … how *old* the thing is" (Karis). **Ages counted from the office's first sheet for each place: the Fallow 61, the Stair 94, the Hall 138, the place behind the iron 206**; the fifth place has two unread signs for its figure ("older than two hundred and six"). **Oldest-last.** The office's run from the fourth place to the fifth is "three days past the iron, a little less"; its compass point and its figure in lengths have not been said aloud. The fourth line of the leaf's list: the mark, over *those who are kindled* and *what is set*, level; *three*. Karis has said none of the list's numbers aloud and five of its nine lines are unturned. **Nothing joins this to lamps, sigils, plates, Arbiters or stations**; "four hundred years" stood once, in Cael's log of the 298th, as his own inference — in this movement it may stand only where this packet's plan fixes it. (6) **Hesk's dividers** have been opened twice, by Karis, on Cael's loan; Cael has never opened them. The hide has a clean sheet pinned to its eastern edge with a prick at the divider's point and the pencil line ruled through it and a hand's breadth past. Stake thirty-two is in the tarred case, never driven. (7) **Oryn** knows the two self-readings, the eleventh and the twelfth; her ruling was "not on my plank". **Her finding** ("There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow* …") is known to Cael and Lira. **Cael's own — the twelfth turned inward unbidden under her hands: *still*, then *set* — is told to NO ONE**, and the next word was not let come; Lira knows only that something unasked came and is waiting; the log holds four reasons and the ruling *hold*. Oryn has not heard the leaf ("Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."). Cleon's warning has "begun to lean". She walks east in the middle of the file with the mule, on nobody's count: three holds owed on her round; "I'm a stop on my own route." (8) **Bodies at dawn on the 299th:** Brom's left shoulder mended, the right re-tied, both arms to shoulder height; Lira's arm released ("It's an arm."); Karis's stitches out, linen on, "Write. Don't lean."; Teague's right wrist in linen under the leather. (9) **Watchers:** a horseman a mile behind on the 296th and a riderless horse in the western alders on the 297th; nothing seen east of the river; no face, name or base. (10) **Seln's case is "shut"** — never write "unopened" or "locked … unopened" (this packet's cutaway note says so and is overridden here); on his chest; contents unnamed; no count of years printed.
