    32	    - **Win sentence, verbatim, once.**
    33	    - *Costs carried forward.* The broad man's right shin, broken in the sink's bed (his good leg). Teague's right arm, wrist and elbow. Brom's breastbone and forearm ("a week of colours"). Cael's left collar-bone, a stave's bruise. A crossbow's stock, split.
    34	12. **Inside the line (who, how long).** The five are inside from the crossing to the last hood: by Cael's reckoning about three minutes — sixty-odd strides at a walk, eleven seconds standing at the pinch, and the time that seven take to go through a gap singly. Nothing is opened. The four with Paths are without them for the whole of it; Vastin's sigil is out for the first time in his life. They come out over the irons at the pinch.
    35	13. **After.** The leg: a fall of rock at the shelf's west end lets the healers down into the bed. Oryn asks and has her answer in a word that does not carry to Cael; the older healer draws the leg straight on her board; Oryn knits it and is grey for a quarter of an hour; **the two healers nod.** Teague's arm: **[[TIER-B: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint. That's not a healer's opinion. That's a fact about a line." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that now,"]]** (the third line is Oryn's by §13; the first two are not pinned). Brom's bill. Cael tells Lira first ("Thirteenth. His. A line."), then the other four of the six, and Oryn at the irons. **Teague is not told**: a second debt of the same kind as the first.
    36	14. **Teague's cutaway (the hut; two scenes).** He counts four by their breathing. The bow's leg on the old woman's board. The boy asleep sitting up with the cloth in his fist. What the watch left under the hide: a bundle of new irons stamped thirty-four with the stroke and bar, a mallet, a cord knotted at the fives, bolts with no fletcher's thread, a keg of water, meal. Why he did not turn. What he saw the boy with the book do at his left for three breaths (a stave, and nothing else). **Nothing of the mechanism and no suspicion of it; the boy is "the boy".**
    37	15. **The Span at noon.** Down the bowl inside the line: Cael, Karis, Lira, Brom, Seln and Vastin; Oryn at the irons with two fingers on Brom's wrist as he crosses ("Four. The same."). An arch on two piers over the sink, all of the grey, no join. No steps: the grey comes up out of the turf on either hand as a road rises, a cart wide, with no kerb, to a crown and down again. **Nothing happens on the crown.** The thirteenth listens at the grey underfoot (nothing goes into it) and the old three ribs ache where the line would come out. The view east: hills, and a notch, low and square. The piers' inner faces, reached from the sink's bed by a rib of rock, are cut in courses; Karis copies nine sheets. **The row counts one short for Cael, twice** (the Book 11 plant), and whole when Lira counts beside him; entered, ruling *hold*. Karis reads the one word that she can turn on the west pier: **[[TIER-B: the bearing runs "Through"]]**. The name: Teague has heard carters on a salt road two days north call the thing that they see from far off "the Sunken Span" (flag).
    38	16. **The 304th's log:** my head line (day, place, purse 123, Vastin twenty-five); **the S19 log, verbatim, in italics, once** (it holds the rate line; its "Tomorrow" is the source's and is flagged — the office's run is three days, a little less); then my count line with the arithmetic (thirty-three; thirteen).
    39	17. **The 305th.** East along the bearing from the fence's far side; two men on sticks; shale country, stepped; camp by the middle of the afternoon on a shelf of shale under a step as high as a man, with the notch four or five miles off. Seln goes on alone to look at it.
    40	18. **The blanket (order of work; mine).** Brom's blanket, on the flat of the shelf, twenty yards from the fire and upwind; Karis, Cael, Lira, Brom and Vastin; Seln when he returns. In the middle the hide with its pinned sheet, the brass on the pencil line; round it, each turned to lie as its stone lay, north to north: one sheet from each of the three floors and the nine of the piers; at the head the flat with its six rows; at the foot her notebook open at the list, Cleon's roll, the sheet of three boxes; under a pebble at one corner the fair copy from Cael's coat, folded, not opened. **The rows lean along the bearing:** a sign that bears heads every run, so each run has a head and a tail; laid as they lay, every run on that blanket has its head to the west and its tail to the east, along the brass. (The twelfth sees the same thing, unbidden, and Cael looks at the brass instead.) **The point:** the two signs in the fifth place's corner are a year in the old town's count, the count in which the head of a certain skin is dated; she lays the one against the other without saying the figure until the close. **The thumbnail circle** goes round the divider's prick.
    41	19. **The lamps finding (Karis's; Tier A 8, verbatim, once).** Its ground on the page: at the Stair and the Fallow and the hall, and yesterday at the irons, every sigil went at the same stride, whole, and came back whole — a Wind of the first rank, an Ember of the third, a boy, and a man who was at the top of the ladder for forty years; no dimming, no order by strength. Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" (pinned; placed). Karis: the ruler rule (Tier B, verbatim). Two pages; the second has nothing on it. **Vastin's third "Noted."** Cael sees the foot of the second row, where a technician's sheet lies, and does not add a third page; Seln's eyes rest there once; neither speaks.
    42	20. **The directive and the objection (Tier A 7).** Vastin, reading the sixth and oldest row through for the first time, finds two slips pinned inside its tape under two seals: both texts read out by him, verbatim; then his three sentences and "That's a crack." (pinned; placed). **[[TIER-B: "The Compact … Yes. Part of it."]]** He does not name the seals; nobody presses him; it is not pried.
    43	21. **One fire.** The broad man is brought to it on the old woman's staff and a cut stick; Vastin, on his, moves his own stick's foot a hand to the left to make room for the other, and says a thing about the ground; **the broad man: "Aye."** (his first word to any of the six). **The healers' third exchange:** Oryn's hands inside the older healer's binding on the shin while the older woman holds the turns open; no word.
    44	22. **Force, dry.** Behind the step, at dusk, out of the fire's sight: heel on a rib of shale, palm on a slab; the line set joint by joint as he saw it set twice. The thirteenth listens and finds both ends. The ribs warn: the line would come out there, short of the hand. He takes his palm away. Trial; not counted. Lira saw. Reasons: a thing that has never been fired is not tried first beside a camp; and its owner is forty yards off with his arm on a board, and has not been told.
    45	23. **Karis's cutaway (two scenes), the night after.** The refusal held in her own head. She knows that a sentence exists; she knows how long it is (six words), as she once knew the length of a word under a glove; she does not let it be said, and she does not write it. Nothing in her head lays the one page on the other.
    46	24. **Seln on the pass:** "I looked at it." (pinned; placed). A notch, low and square; he did not like it; he will look again from nearer. **The close:** **[[TIER-B: the S20 close]]**, then the fixed last line of narration, verbatim.
