   113	3. **Teague, two (cutaway).** Why he did not turn; the boy asleep with the cloth; the one with the book and a stave.
   114	4. **Down the bowl.** Oryn at the irons ("Four. The same."); the arch; the road that rises; the crown. Nothing.
