   146	- **Decision 13 changed: Oryn is not told of the thirteenth in this movement.** At the irons at noon on the 304th she sees that Cael has something and will not be told "across a row of iron"; an old man is five feet off. Lira is told first, in three words (51.1); Brom has it from her and says so behind the step (53.2). Karis and Seln have it from Lira or from the log.
   147	- **Decision 18 changed: "the rows lean along the bearing"** rests on the twelfth's one unbidden glance over fourteen sheets that Karis had already laid as their walls stood, entered by her as his and as unchecked. I dropped her head-west / tail-east proof: it would have made the south wall's runs read from right to left, against the lamp's rule in the closed Deepstacks chapters (all the looking runs from the low left upward to the right).
   148	- **Decision 19 changed: Seln is not at the blanket** (he has gone to look at the gap), so no glance passes between him and Cael over the second row; Cael keeps his third page alone.
